Hannah James is a 52-year-old female who presents to the clinic for follow-up of high blood sugar. She reports she has been eating a lot of sweets recently due to the holidays. She states she felt fine initially, but over the past week she has been feeling light-headed and seeing spots and was dizzy. She states she was treated in the emergency room and was given fluids and advised to cut out sweets and resume her normal diet. She states that she is having a hard time with this due to her family members being big bakers. She is here to follow up to ensure she is nipping the high blood sugar in the bud.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Reports feeling light-headed and dizzy.
• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or shortness of breath. She does have a history of atrial fibrillation.
• Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath.
• Gastrointestinal: Denies abdominal pain. She has a history of gastroesophageal reflux disease and is currently on Protonix 40 mg once a day.
