• Abdomen: Soft, no tenderness, no organomegaly, no hepatosplenomegaly.
• Extremities: No edema.

RESULTS

• Blood glucose: Elevated.
• Hemoglobin A1c: Elevated.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

High blood sugar.

• Medical Reasoning: The patient presents with a history of high blood sugar. Her blood sugar and hemoglobin A1c are elevated. She has a history of atrial fibrillation and gastroesophageal reflux disease.

• Medical Treatment: We will order a complete metabolic panel to evaluate for diabetes. We will start her on metformin 500 mg twice a day. We will hold off on insulin until we have the results of the autoimmune labs.

• Patient Education and Counseling: The patient was advised to avoid foods high in sugar. The nurse will provide education on how to do blood sugar testing with the glucometer provided.

