summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Full spectrum std testing.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Ross is a 24-year-old female who presents to the clinic today for a full spectrum std testing. She reports a change in discharge, odor, and discomfort in her vaginal region. She states the right side of her vagina is becoming painful. She denies fevers or chills. She recently learned that her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people and she wants to be evaluated for all stds.

The patient reports that she has been experiencing some discharge, which is different in color and consistency than what she is used to. She also notes that the right side of her vagina has been sore and has not improved. She denies any fevers or chills.

Ms. Ross has a history of irregular pap smears in the past, but her last pap smear was normal 6 months ago.

MEDICAL HISTORY

Medical Reasoning

Ms. Ross is a 24-year-old female who presents today for full spectrum std testing. She reports symptoms of discomfort, a change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. She denies fevers or chills. She recently learned that her sexual partner has been in sexual encounters with other people, and she wants to be evaluated for all stds.

The patient's symptoms are concerning for stds, particularly chlamydia, gonorrhea, and trichomoniasis. The patient has a history of irregular pap smears in the past, but her last pap smear was normal 6 months ago.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Examination of the Genitourinary System

Pelvic exam demonstrates no external lesions. Normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge, with normal color and smell. Cervix is normal. Vaginal wall is normal. No cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted. Swabs were done for std testing.

RESULTS

Ms. Ross had std testing done today for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, and blood was drawn for syphilis, hiv and hepatitis c. Some of these tests will take longer than others. We will call you if we see anything, but if you have not heard anything, you can call us in 3 days for results.

ASSESSMENT

Ms. Ross is positive for being high risk due to an abnormal pap smear in the past and the recent discovery of her sexual partner having multiple partners.

PLAN

The patient was advised to return for follow up if she has any further symptoms. If everything is normal, she will return for her next annual checkup. }}<|eot_id|>
