summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Acne.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Jacqueline Miller is a 31-year-old female who presents today for follow-up of her acne. She reports that she has been doing well on her previous medications, but she has plateaued and has had a small amount of residual rash. She was taking doxycycline 100 mg once a day and was experiencing a plateau. She states that she has been using the sulfacetamide wash twice a day and the metro cream after washing. She also states that she has been using it once a day and it has been helping. She is not breastfeeding.

The patient is unsure of the duration of her acne. She states that she has had acne on and off for as long as she can remember. She has tried a variety of treatments in the past, including antibiotics and retinoids, which have not been effective. She has been using the sulfacetamide wash and the metro cream for the past 2 weeks.

MEDICATIONS

• Doxycycline 100 mg once a day.

SOCIAL HISTORY

• Patient is not currently breastfeeding.

VITALS

• Temperature: Not recorded.
• Blood pressure: Not recorded.
• Heart rate: Not recorded.
• Respiratory rate: Not recorded.
• Saturation: Not recorded.
• Height: Not recorded.
• Weight: Not recorded.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Fitzpatrick skin type IV. 
• Erythematous papules on the bilateral medial cheeks and redness around and underneath the nostrils. No other lesions.

ASSESSMENT

• Perioral dermatitis.
• Rosacea, including ocular rosacea.

PLAN

I advised the patient to continue using the sulfacetamide wash twice a day and to apply the metro cream once a day. I recommended increasing the doxycycline to 100 mg twice a day. I also advised her to continue the use of the face wash and the metro cream. I explained that she can use the tacrolimus ointment if she wants to try it. I also explained that she can continue using the doxycycline for another week and then stop. I provided her with a few samples of vanicream for moisturizer. I advised her to stay away from any anti-aging or plant-based products. I will see her again in 4 weeks for follow-up.

INSTRUCTIONS

• Continue to use the sulfacetamide wash twice a day.
• Continue to use the metro cream once a day.
• Increase the doxycycline to 100 mg twice a day.
• Use the tacrolimus ointment once a day until the rash is gone, then once a day for another week before stopping.
• Continue to use the face wash and the metro cream after the rash is gone.
• Use vanicream for moisturizer.
• Stay away from anti-aging or plant-based products.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
