Neck: No jugular venous distention.
CV: 3/6 systolic ejection murmur heard at the left base. No carotid bruits appreciated.
Lungs: Clear bilaterally.
Extremities: 1+ pitting edema of the right lower extremity. Right radial artery pulses are palpable.
Lower extremities: No lower extremity edema.

RESULTS

EKG: Normal sinus rhythm with good R wave progression. Evolutionary changes expected after STEMI.

ECHO: Reduced ejection fraction of 35%.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

1. Coronary artery disease.
- Medical Reasoning: Patient presents with history of coronary artery disease and currently having an interior STEMI.
- Medical Treatment: Continue aspirin 81 mg daily, brilinta 90 mg twice daily, Lipitor 80 mg daily, Toprol 50 mg daily, metformin, Lasix 40 mg daily, and Aldactone 12.5 mg daily.

2. Newly reduced left ventricular dysfunction and moderate mitral regurgitation.
- Medical Reasoning: Patient has reduced ejection fraction of 35%.
- Medical Treatment: Continue Lipitor 80 mg daily and continue to monitor.

3. Acute heart failure.
- Medical Reasoning: Patient has newly reduced ejection fraction of 35% and moderate mitral regurgitation.
- Medical Treatment: Prescribe Lasix 40 mg daily. Add Aldactone 12.5 mg daily.

4. Hypertension.
- Medical Reasoning: Patient has a history of hypertension.
- Medical Treatment: Continue monitoring. We will repeat another echo in 2 months.

INSTRUCTIONS

Patient will continue to follow up with the clinic in 2 months for a repeat echocardiogram. We will also refer her to cardiac rehabilitation for further education and exercise training. }}<|eot_id|>
