Kyle Smith is a pleasant 32-year-old male who presents to the clinic today with a 2-week history of low back pain. He states that the pain started after lifting a box of books. He denies any prior history of back pain. He reports that the pain is achy and sharp in nature and is located in his low back. The pain does radiate down his left leg. He denies any numbness or tingling in his legs. He denies any loss of sensation or weakness. He denies any loss of control of his bladder or bowels. He states that the pain has gotten worse over time and he has tried taking ibuprofen and Tylenol which sometimes helps. He has not had any surgery for his back before.

The patient reports that he is an Olympic weightlifter with books. He is sedentary and works in a sedentary job. He denies any history of playing sports. He reports that his father has back pain.

