summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Left knee pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Angela Rodriguez is a 35-year-old female who presents to the clinic today for evaluation of left knee pain. She states that she hurt her left knee approximately one week ago while playing with her 5-year-old niece who is learning to ride a bike without training wheels. She states that she fell and twisted her knee in some type of funky way. She denies hearing a pop at the time of injury. She states that she has been limping since the injury and that her pain has not improved. She rates her pain as 4/10 initially but it is getting worse. She has been taking Tylenol and wrapping her knee with Kinesiology tape. She states that the Tylenol helps a little bit but she has to stop taking it every 4 hours. She denies taking ibuprofen due to having a recent ulcer. She reports that her pain is throbbing in nature and that it is worse on the medial aspect of her knee.

PAST HISTORY

Medical Reasoning

The patient has a history of an ulcer.

MEDICATIONS

Tylenol.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Denies fever.
Musculoskeletal: Reports left knee pain.
Neurological: Denies numbness or tingling in the left leg.
Skin: Denies rashes.

PHYSICAL EXAM

MSK
- Examination of the left knee: Examination of the left knee shows moderate swelling, effusion, and pain on flexion and extension. Negative Lachman's test and valgus and varus stress test.

RESULTS

X-rays of the left knee were obtained and are normal.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Ms. Rodriguez is a 35-year-old female who presents with left knee pain. She reports a twisting injury while playing with her 5-year-old niece who is learning to ride a bike without training wheels. She reports pain on the medial aspect of her knee. Examination of her left knee shows moderate swelling, effusion, and pain on flexion and extension. X-rays of her left knee are normal. Given her history of an ulcer, she is unable to take NSAIDs. She is currently taking Tylenol. She is placed in a knee immobilizer and advised to ice the knee 3-4 times a day for 20-30 minutes. She is to take 50 mg of tramadol twice a day. She is advised to avoid running for the next 3 weeks. She is to follow up in 2 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
